# Job Detail Analysis Tab Consistency

When adding or changing a tab under **Job Detail → Analysis** (the Bootstrap nav shared by Metrics, Summary plot, Roofline, Multiprecision Mix, Processes, etc.), align presentation with existing tabs unless there is an explicit product reason not to.

## Plot tabs (Bokeh panels)

Canonical patterns live in **`hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/views/JobDetail.tsx`** → **`renderSinglePlotPanel`** and **`PlotPanel`** → **`BokehEmbed`**.

### Structure

- **Section chrome**: Wrap each chart block in **`job-detail-single-plot-host`** / **`mb-3 w-full`**, **`h3`** title, then **`PlotPanel`** only — no intro paragraph under the title.
- **Embed**: Always **`PlotPanel`** (do not call **`BokehEmbed`** directly from the page for parity).

### Loading / unavailable messaging

- **Unavailable plots**: **`BokehEmbed`** shows the user-visible **`Unavailable — Data not available.`** status line for everyone; staff-only expandable detail uses **`unavailableReason`** from the API (`job_plot_artifacts` / `job_detail_artifacts` style strings — mirror **`Missing … in host_data`** / **`Missing … in job metrics`** phrasing used by summary and roofline builders).
- **Do not** drive multiprecision or other artifact-backed embed **`isLoading`** from **`detailsLoading`** when plot payloads already arrive with **`getJobDetailLight`** — that flashes misleading **Loading …** copy instead of the same unavailable surfacing as Summary/Roofline.
- Progressive **`job_plots`** tabs continue to use **`plots[key].loading`** as **`isLoadingExternal`** on **`PlotPanel`**.

### Regression expectation

Any new plot-class tab needs **`JobDetail.test.tsx`** coverage analogous to existing Summary/Roofline/Multiprecision tests (title + plot panel present; no Host-level plot intro; unavailable messaging stable).

## Non-plot tabs

Follow neighboring tabs for typography (**`h3`** subsection headings), **`text-muted`** empty states (**Data not available.** where tables/lists would render), and role/tabpanel wiring (**`aria-labelledby`** / **`hidden`**).

### Metrics tab source subsections

- Group `metrics_list` rows by API **`type`** into ordered **`h3`** sections inside Shadcn **`Card`** chrome (same rounded family as Job overview): **CPU → GPU → File System → Network → Misc** (map in [`jobMetricSourceSections.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/utils/jobMetricSourceSections.ts)).
- **CPU** includes host CPU/PMC/IMC/DF/RAPL/CHA plus **`host_mem` / `host_numa`**; GPU includes `nvidia_gpu` / `amd_gpu` / **`intel_gpu`** / `gpu`; Network includes IB/OPA/Ethernet/LNET (`host_ib`, `host_opa`, `host_net`, `net`, `host_lnet`, `lnet`).
- **Always show Network** (empty body: muted **Data not available.**). **Hide** empty GPU, File System, and Misc headings.
- Preserve post-merge display order within each section (including combined DP/SP vector-width row under CPU). Two-column tables stay **per section**.

### Resources section Cards

- Wrap Resources blocks in **`Card`** chrome in order **Watt hours → GPU Information → Shared File Systems → Client/Server logs**.
- **GPU Information:** aggregate stats are the main surface; **GPU inventory** is a default-**closed** `Collapsible` under the aggregates.

## Print layout

Job Detail **Print** uses the browser print dialog (`window.print` → Save as PDF). Do **not** add CDN or npm PDF libraries (`jspdf` / `html2canvas`).

- **In-scope surfaces:** Job overview, Full scheduling record, Resources, Metrics, Summary plot, Roofline, Multiprecision Mix.
- **Out of scope:** Processes, Execution and hosts, Device data (mark with **`job-detail-print-out-of-scope`**; do not `keepMounted` for print).
- **Prep:** set **`data-job-detail-print="1"`** on the page wrapper; force-load multiprecision + plots; **`keepMounted`** + mount in-scope **`PlotPanel`**s even when the active tab differs; open scheduling / GPU inventory collapsibles; disable Bokeh viewport defer during prep so embeds can measure.
- **CSS:** screen + `@media print` rules in **`globals.css`** keyed off **`[data-job-detail-print]`** (override Base UI **`[hidden]`** on in-scope panels with `display: block !important`; hide chrome, tablist, Print button, out-of-scope panels).
- **Cleanup:** `afterprint` (plus a safety timeout) clears print layout so normal tab lazy-mount resumes.
- **Tests:** **`JobDetail.test.tsx`** + **`job-detail-print.ts`** helpers; researcher doc per **`researcher-job-detail-doc-sync.mdc`**.

